    {
      "post_id": 22104,
      "author_username": "meizzwang",
      "author_user_id": 11,
      "timestamp_iso": "2015-09-28T22:46:22+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1443480382000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Sept 28, 2015 17:46:22 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Some more clone F's.  They didn't get as fat as I was hoping for, but still, these are really beautiful year after year.  Photos taken 9/25/15:<br/><img src=\"https://farm6.staticflickr.com/5833/21794496725_b8373c1a0e_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://farm6.staticflickr.com/5665/21770336556_8a8998af17_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>That fat trap in the middle is clone F, it definitely stands out of the crowd...although the crowd is also pretty crazy:<br/><img src=\"https://farm1.staticflickr.com/685/21171763104_c066fee7fe_c.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>",
      "body_text": "Some more clone F's.  They didn't get as fat as I was hoping for, but still, these are really beautiful year after year.  Photos taken 9/25/15:\nThat fat trap in the middle is clone F, it definitely stands out of the crowd...although the crowd is also pretty crazy:",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://farm6.staticflickr.com/5833/21794496725_b8373c1a0e_c.jpg",
        "https://farm6.staticflickr.com/5665/21770336556_8a8998af17_c.jpg",
        "https://farm1.staticflickr.com/685/21171763104_c066fee7fe_c.jpg"
      ],
      "quoted_post_ids": []
    },
    {
      "post_id": 22265,
      "author_username": "calen",
      "author_user_id": 155,
      "timestamp_iso": "2015-10-02T21:12:38+00:00",
      "timestamp_epoch_ms": 1443820358000,
      "timestamp_raw": "Oct 2, 2015 16:12:38 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "Daaaamn Mike! Looking just amazing, as usual. One day I will have a mass of these babies a la Wang and John Hummer I swear! Such an incredible display. Here's my clone F these days. For whatever reason it kinda held out on me the last 2 seasons and didn't produce a really crazy fall show, but this year it is going nuts! I think it needed some time to establish and probably benefited from the larger pot I put it in this spring. Any who, first pic taken about a week ago as fall trape still inflating. Note the late summer \"pre-fall\" traps that are pretty darn nice but not quite as robust as the true fall crop coming in close on their heels:<br/><a href=\"http://s1329.photobucket.com/user/calenhall/media/Mobile%20Uploads/image_zpsdgpdbiwg.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1329.photobucket.com/albums/w549/calenhall/Mobile%20Uploads/image_zpsdgpdbiwg.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a><br/>The fall traps, pics taken today. Blinding, bulbous, and pushing 30\". Not bad!<br/><a href=\"http://s1329.photobucket.com/user/calenhall/media/Mobile%20Uploads/image_zps2wlcd0sq.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1329.photobucket.com/albums/w549/calenhall/Mobile%20Uploads/image_zps2wlcd0sq.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a><br/>The copper blush can be very prominent on fresh traps, but fades in a week or so.<br/><a href=\"http://s1329.photobucket.com/user/calenhall/media/Mobile%20Uploads/image_zpsde9uprra.jpg.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://i1329.photobucket.com/albums/w549/calenhall/Mobile%20Uploads/image_zpsde9uprra.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/></a><br/>",
      "body_text": "Daaaamn Mike! Looking just amazing, as usual. One day I will have a mass of these babies a la Wang and John Hummer I swear! Such an incredible display. Here's my clone F these days. For whatever reason it kinda held out on me the last 2 seasons and didn't produce a really crazy fall show, but this year it is going nuts! I think it needed some time to establish and probably benefited from the larger pot I put it in this spring. Any who, first pic taken about a week ago as fall trape still inflating. Note the late summer \"pre-fall\" traps that are pretty darn nice but not quite as robust as the true fall crop coming in close on their heels:\nThe fall traps, pics taken today. Blinding, bulbous, and pushing 30\". Not bad!\nThe copper blush can be very prominent on fresh traps, but fades in a week or so.",
      "image_urls": [
        "http://i1329.photobucket.com/albums/w549/calenhall/Mobile%20Uploads/image_zpsdgpdbiwg.jpg",
